    <h2 id="about-h" class="display glitch" data-text="About me" data-reveal>About me</h2>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:1">I was a writer before I was a developer. I built worlds first: universes, power systems, characters with flaws they can’t outrun. Then I found code, and started building things that run instead of things you read.</p>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:2">Now I’m a third-year IT student at Saint Louis University and a full-stack developer who leans back end: APIs, data models, the logic that has to hold up once real people use it. I still care how the front end feels. Java was my first language; these days it’s mostly Python and TypeScript, with some Rust.</p>
    <p data-reveal style="--d:3">The worldbuilding never left. It’s why I think in systems, rules and edge cases. Next, I’m learning AI engineering properly, from the ground up.</p>
